cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the results it produces, please cite the associated paper."
title: "Placement-specific inertial-axis reduction for wearable gym exercise recognition"
abstract: >-
  Evaluation of 30 axis configurations, from the full six-axis inertial set
  through drop-one subsets, same-sensor and mixed accelerometer-gyroscope
  pairs, pure triples and single axes, on the public RecGym dataset at three
  body positions (wrist, pocket, calf), scored by macro-F1 under
  leave-one-subject-out validation. Axis-level reduction is shown to be a
  placement-specific decision rather than a universal saving.
